NAME
  dpkg - install, remove, and inspect Freax packages

SYNOPSIS
  dpkg -i PACKAGE.fpkg...
  dpkg --unpack PACKAGE.fpkg...
  dpkg --configure PACKAGE...
  dpkg --configure -a
  dpkg -r PACKAGE...
  dpkg -P PACKAGE...
  dpkg -l [PATTERN]
  dpkg -L PACKAGE
  dpkg -S PATH
  dpkg -s PACKAGE

DESCRIPTION
  dpkg is the low-level package tool. It unpacks .fpkg archives, runs
  maintainer scripts, records what is installed in
  /var/lib/dpkg/status, and removes packages. It performs no dependency
  resolution, does not download anything, and does not consult a
  repository; those jobs belong to apt. Use dpkg -i to install a local
  archive, and apt to install by name.

  A package moves through unpacking and configuration. It is not
  considered installed until --configure has run the packaged postinst
  script. dpkg records states such as installed, unpacked,
  half-configured, half-installed, config-files, and not-installed so
  that an interrupted operation can be resumed.

  dpkg takes a lock at /var/lib/dpkg/lock while it changes the database;
  concurrent dpkg operations fail rather than corrupt it.

COMMANDS
  -i, --install PACKAGE.fpkg...
    Unpack each archive and then configure it. This is the normal way to
    install a local file.
  --unpack PACKAGE.fpkg...
    Unpack each archive without configuring it.
  --configure PACKAGE...
    Configure one or more already-unpacked packages by running their
    postinst scripts.
  --configure -a
    Configure every package that is unpacked but not yet configured.
  -r, --remove PACKAGE...
    Remove packages. Files listed by the package are deleted, but
    conffiles are kept and the package is left in the config-files state.
    The prerm and postrm scripts run with the "remove" action.
  -P, --purge PACKAGE...
    Remove packages and delete their conffiles as well. The postrm
    script runs with the "purge" action.
  -l, --list [PATTERN]
    List packages known to dpkg with their state and short description.
    A PATTERN filters by name. With no pattern, everything is listed.
  -L, --listfiles PACKAGE
    List the files owned by an installed package, one absolute path per
    line.
  -S, --search PATH
    Show which installed package owns PATH.
  -s, --status PACKAGE
    Print the full control fields and status of a package.
  --get-selections
    Print every package and its selection state.
  --print-architecture
    Print the architecture dpkg targets (always all on Freax).
  --version
    Print the dpkg version.
  -h, --help
    Print usage.

FILES
  /var/lib/dpkg/status
  /var/lib/dpkg/lock
  /var/lib/dpkg/info/<package>.list
  /var/lib/dpkg/info/<package>.sha256sums
  /var/lib/dpkg/info/<package>.conffiles
  /var/lib/dpkg/info/<package>.preinst|postinst|prerm|postrm

EXAMPLES
  dpkg -i hello_1.0_all.fpkg
    Install a local archive.

  dpkg --configure -a
    Finish packages left half-configured by an interrupted operation.

  dpkg -l hello
    Show whether hello is installed.

  dpkg -L hello
    List the files hello installed.

  dpkg -S /bin/hello
    Show which package owns /bin/hello.

  dpkg -P hello
    Remove hello and its conffiles.